    "evidence_text": " She competed for Team Finland at the 2012 Summer Olympics.\n\n2004 European Short Course Swimming Championships\n\n The meet featured teams from Europe, swimming in 38 short course events.\n\n It was held in Vienna's arena (Wiener Stadthalle), in a temporary pool.\n\nEuropean Short Course Swimming Championships\n\n The meet has traditionally been held in the beginning of December.\n\n Annual until 2013, the event now occurs in odd years.\n\nSwedish Short Course Swimming Championships\n\n The championships sometimes also works as trials for the World Championships and European Short Course Swimming Championships.\n\n Swimmers representing Swedish swim teams may participate.\n\nRoyal Arena\n\n The ground was broken for construction on 26 June 2013 and the arena opened in February 2017.\n\n2010 European Short Course Swimming Championships\n\n2007 European Short Course Swimming Championships\n\n2017 European Short Course Swimming Championships\n\nThe 2017 European Short Course Swimming Championships will take place in Copenhagen, Denmark.\n\n The meet will be held in the Royal Arena, which was finished in early 2017.\n\nEsther Baron\n\n While winning the short course championship in 2006 she set a new European record.",
